Bedrock 1.26.51.1 supplies separate emitter callbacks at 1462a3690,
1462a3710, 1462a3790 and 1462a3870. Independent execution supplies 52
schedules, 364 updates and 288 distance predicates. Probes supply actor,
resource, query and event-receipt boundaries. Automatic births and reset
random registration are outside these cases. Child scheduling, complete
expression context and visible parity remain unverified. Native binaries,
assets and fixtures stay private. Production needs no installed game.

Keep typed Program evaluation in the shared appearance MoLang evaluator.
The actor graph and its long-script budget test already belong to this
feature, so they must not depend on a helper introduced by later server
player controller support. Move the existing implementation here without
changing full-stack behavior or adding a compatibility method.

Resolve particle sound_effect actions as individual level sound events,
then decode their configured catalog samples through the existing PCM
player. Preserve particle, sound, expression and log order. Unknown
target event names suppress sound without suppressing other leaf actions.
Acquire root sounds.json from the licensed package and invalidate older
asset caches. Read generic configurations in pack order, with group
ranges, event overrides, ASCII name normalization and native scalar
conversions. Sample pitch before volume using paired unsigned random
draws and triangular float32 arithmetic. Skip draws for constant ranges,
clamp command volume to one and suppress zero-volume requests.

Target Bedrock 1.26.51.1 native execution verifies 56 dispatch cases,
34 numeric/object/array range cases, 70 sampling cases and nine command
volume cases. Probes supply JSON lookup, prepared graph/command fields,
random draws and receipt boundaries. Native ASCII normalization and
string range parsing are inspected evidence. Accepted name membership
comes from ViaBedrock's protocol 2193 target data, including null mappings.
These checks do not establish seeded RNG, audible mixing, captions,
server/native comparisons or a complete level-event context resolver.
Fresh licensed package extraction includes the root sound tables; the
three official particle drip events resolve their configured PCM samples.

Render all eleven Bedrock 1.26.51 billboard facing modes with explicit
columns instead of a quaternion-only quad. Preserve custom world direction,
independently normalized locator columns, reflected and sheared planes,
and the target's vertical direction boundaries. Non-finite native axes
suppress that quad before Java vertex submission.

The owned 1.26.51.1 executable's facing name table and CPU quad builder
establish mode selection and orientation. Independent native instruction
execution covers 286 facing branch cases, 32 emitter basis cases, and 144
world-direction interpolation/normalization cases. These prepared probes
exclude camera selection, vertex submission, visible output, and complete
frame interpolation. The licensed package shaders receive finished vertices;
private shaders, executables, account licenses, and fixtures are not shipped.

Another 440 cases execute the native spin matrix multiplication after each
facing branch, with imported float32 cosf/sinf results supplied. Use the
resulting axes for both quad corners and frustum bounds so sheared planes
remain visible. Each frame owns its world direction and immutable matrix.

The owned Bedrock 1.26.51.1 actor-bound child factory starts with an
identity transform and binds the actor/locator separately. Preserve the
full event matrix only for ordinary emitters and unbound fallbacks, so a
collision rotation cannot rotate a bound child's locator a second time.
Native factory wrappers and the binding setter execute in 24 prepared
cases. Resource lookup, allocation/constructor, initialized matrix
constants, binding liveness, memcpy and cleanup boundaries are supplied;
actor query evaluation, branch selection and visible output remain outside
these fixtures. Add production comparisons and a scaled-locator regression.

Refresh particle actor query bindings before child initialization, updates,
and render expressions without sharing the parent's Molang variables.
Keep the target's generic particle animation clock fields separate from
actor animation time. Sample emitter camera distance from its cached origin,
and preserve native float32 velocity scaling in the ground-speed query.

The owned Bedrock 1.26.51.1 context refresh and initialization gate execute
in 54 prepared cases. Native scalar query callbacks execute with supplied
actor resolution, level access, variable storage, expression callbacks and
motion-component lookup. These cases establish query bindings and context
fields; live/offscreen actor updates, scheduling and visible playback still
need comparisons. Sample player queries during emotes as well as base poses.

The native actor-present child dispatcher passes the parent's base origin
as binding metadata while constructing the child at identity. Apply that
offset only to actor fallback translation, not resolved locators. Replace
the binding offset for each generation instead of accumulating ancestors.

Execute the full dispatcher, binding setter, initialization gate and query
refresh in 48 prepared cases, including absent, present, removed and
missing-component actors. The latter two retain registry bindings and
suppress child initialization; that registry-only Java adapter remains
incomplete. Resource/constructor fields, binding getters, weak registry
resolution, expression callbacks and variable access are supplied boundaries.
Rework the 192 matrix comparisons to exercise the production offset adapter
and add a child/grandchild placement regression. Scheduling and native
visible comparisons remain separate work.

Distinguish live actor objects from retained registry components in particle
attachments. The target registry path interpolates position and wrapped yaw,
uses registry locators, and ignores the actor binding offset in its position
fallback. Keep the network owner identity as the retained component lifetime
boundary and invalidate replacement identities.

Registry-only bound children retain parent construction origin and binding
metadata, while invalid actor contexts suppress child initialization and
local-position rendering. Expire before the first update but preserve its
native births; clear local populations on subsequent invalid updates and
allow world-space particles to drain. Keep binding presence separate from
actor query validity.

Execute 384 complete native registry matrix cases, 12 schedules with 36
updates, and eight render-entry gates. The prior 48 combined dispatcher
cases now compare registry child frames and initialization suppression.
Weak registry resolvers, binding/resource getters, imported math/byte
comparison, prepared component tables, particle allocation/initial values
and expression receipts are supplied boundaries. Live component lifetime,
asynchronous child dispatch and visible native comparisons remain unverified.

Preload reachable child particle assets before root playback and dispatch
event children inline before source expressions. Keep initialization in
the child's own Molang context. Bound dependency discovery, deduplicate
shared effects, and terminate cycles. Refresh population limits during
births and include manual children in the current render extraction.

The 48 target dispatcher/context receipts verify initialization order.
Native cold-load timing, first update ordering for new emitters, live
component lifetime, and visible playback still need comparisons.

Match the target particle manager's update batch membership. Prune dead
emitters before batch capture, replace each removed entry with the last
entry, and retain emitters that die during the update until a later batch.
Children appended by update callbacks wait for the next captured batch.

The complete manager and its native expiry/population getters execute in
16 prepared schedules covering 80 frames. Platform clocks, ambient grid,
metrics, and emitter identity/update/destructor callbacks are supplied.
Live timing, real native emitter updates, and visible playback remain open.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 registers particle count callbacks 14065a9e0 through
14065ab60. Effect emitter counts read the manager's live identifier map;
total emitter counts read its registered vector size. Effect and total
particle counts read populations published after a complete update batch.
Sample each emitter's size immediately after its update. Inline child
births change emitter counts immediately; their particles enter published
counts only when the child belongs to an update batch. Later callbacks
cannot revise an earlier emitter's sampled population.

The first creation expression has no emitter owner in its query context.
Install zero count bindings for that expression, then retain live bindings
through child initialization, updates, loop restarts and particle copies.
Aggregate matching definition identifiers across resource libraries and
clear all counters when playback stops.

Independent execution verifies 84 prepared scalar cases with 672 callback
calls, four manager frames with 36 count receipts, and two restart context
cases. Native count readers, manager pruning and publication, and restart
component dispatch execute. Platform access, map allocation, factory
registration, emitter updates, expression callbacks and random variable
registration are supplied or skipped boundaries. Production tests compare
count publication and Molang lifecycle behavior. Full constructor execution,
client frame gates, complete query context and visible playback remain
unverified; these checks do not establish full particle or skin parity.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 registers spellcolor through functor 14e7ff500 and
callback 14220f9d0. Read actor metadata slot 77 only when its type is Int
(2). Return RGBA structure fields as float32 byte channels divided by 255;
missing actors, entries and matching types return zero channels. This
matches DATA_SPELL_CASTING_COLOR in the target ViaBedrock protocol 2193.

Publish immutable spell color snapshots after network metadata updates.
Bind queries to the original network actor so replacement identities do
not inherit its color. Existing particles read current snapshots without
waiting for another actor render. Initial emitter creation has no actor
context and sees zero; refreshed child contexts consume the live color.
Expose the query as a Molang structure, including nested property access,
explicit query calls and variable copies, and feed it into particle tint.

Independent native execution verifies 1504 scalar cases, all 256 byte
values in each channel, and 60 prepared initialization/context cases.
Actor and metadata gates and float32 conversion execute. Metadata type,
color structure allocation/cleanup, actor/resource lookup and expression
callbacks are supplied. Production tests execute actual Molang and tint
render inputs, snapshots, actor removal and replacement. Live network
captures, native object property lookup, tint quantization and visible
